powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "description": "Allowlist of columns the browser may write on contact. Four trigger columns: al_claimrequest, which carries the id of the case being claimed (AD-076); al_signoffrequest, which carries the T&C attestation as JSON (AD-099); al_regraderequest, which carries the final regraded outcome as JSON (OD-041); and al_caseheaderrequest, which carries a Tax checker's edit of the two Tax team header fields as JSON (2026-09-13). Each is acted on by its own plug-in, which checks the contact's web role server-side - the allowlist is per table, not per role, so a reviewer who may write the claim request cannot sign off or regrade through the others. Everything a contact record actually holds - name, email, the web roles - stays off this list, so exposing contact to the Web API grants the page these four writes and nothing else.",
  "value": "al_claimrequest,al_signoffrequest,al_regraderequest,al_caseheaderrequest"
}
